---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import Counter from '../components/Counter.astro';
import { models, getModel, bothUnits } from '../data/models';

import heroImg from '../assets/panel-large.jpg';
import storyImg from '../assets/regera.jpg';

/* Every figure quoted below is pulled from src/data/models.ts. The old
   About page retyped its own numbers and ended up contradicting the
   Collection page by 30 km/h. */
const agera = getModel('agera')!;
const regera = getModel('regera')!;
const gemera = getModel('gemera')!;
const jesko = getModel('jesko')!;

const record = agera.headline.topSpeed;

const FOUNDED = 1994;
const yearsRunning = new Date().getFullYear() - FOUNDED;

/* Principles, not "values" — these describe how the cars are made rather
   than making claims on the company's behalf. */
const principles = [
  {
    n: '01',
    title: 'Make it, don’t buy it',
    body:
      'Engines, transmissions, carbon tubs, wheels. When a supplier’s catalogue sets the ceiling, the part gets designed in-house instead — which is slow, expensive, and the reason the cars are what they are.',
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    title: 'Patents before parts',
    body:
      'Freevalve’s camshaft-less actuation, Direct Drive, the Triplex rear suspension, the dihedral synchro-helix door. Each one started as a problem nobody sold an answer to.',
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    title: 'Records as evidence',
    body:
      'Top-speed runs are made in both directions on a closed road and averaged, with independent timing equipment. That turns the headline number into a test result rather than a claim.',
  },
];

/* Milestones. Bodies interpolate the shared spec data so a figure can only
   ever be edited in one place. */
const milestones = [
  {
    year: '1994',
    title: 'One founder, no factory',
    body:
      'Christian von Koenigsegg starts the company at twenty-two, on the premise that the car he wants does not exist and the shortest route to it is building the firm that makes it. A running prototype follows two years later.',
  },
  {
    year: '2002',
    title: 'The CC8S leaves the workshop',
    body:
      'Eight years in, the first Koenigsegg a customer could actually buy. A handful were built — enough to establish that a workshop in southern Sweden could sit at the same table as Modena and Woking.',
  },
  {
    year: '2015',
    title: 'The Regera is unveiled',
    body: `Koenigsegg Direct Drive replaces the transmission with a single fixed ratio to the rear axle, leaving three electric motors to supply the torque the missing gears would have found. ${regera.headline.power.value} ${regera.headline.power.unit}, and no shift at all. Shown at Geneva in 2015; customer cars ran ${regera.years}.`,
  },
  {
    year: '2017',
    title: 'Nevada, both ways',
    body: `On a closed stretch of State Route 160, an Agera RS averaged ${bothUnits(record)} across two passes in opposite directions — at the time the highest verified average top speed recorded by a production car.`,
  },
  {
    year: '2020',
    title: 'Two directions at once',
    body: `The Gemera arrives as a four-seat Mega-GT rated at ${gemera.headline.power.value} ${gemera.headline.power.unit}, while the ${jesko.fullName} goes the other way entirely: wings stripped, underbody sealed, shaped around the lowest drag the company has measured.`,
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About this concept build"
  description="An independent look at Koenigsegg — a Swedish workshop that builds its own engines, transmissions and records. Part of a fan-made concept site."
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow={`Est. ${FOUNDED}`}
    title="Built the"
    titleAccent="hard way"
    lede="Three decades of a small Swedish workshop solving problems the rest of the industry had quietly agreed to stop asking about."
    image={heroImg}
    imageAlt="A grey Koenigsegg Gemera parked side-on against a dark quarried rock face"
    size="compact"
    align="center"
  />

  <!-- ── Story ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section--deep" aria-labelledby="story-heading">
    <div class="container story">
      <div class="story__text reveal">
        <SectionHeader id="story-heading"
          eyebrow="The story"
          title="A workshop that decided to build everything itself"
          as="h2"
          align="start"
        />

        <p class="story__lead">
          Koenigsegg is what happens when someone concludes that the car they want does not
          exist, and that founding a company is a reasonable way to fix that.
        </p>

        <p>
          The first prototype ran in 1996. It took until 2002 for a customer car to leave the
          building. Six years between a running chassis and a sale is not how the industry
          works, and it set the pattern for everything after it: given the choice between
          ordering a component and designing one, Ängelholm has almost always designed one.
        </p>

        <p>
          A fire destroyed the original premises in 2003. The company moved into decommissioned
          hangars at a former air force base outside Ängelholm and took the resident fighter
          squadron’s ghost as its emblem — one of the few badges in the business with a real
          story behind it.
        </p>

        <p>
          What follows from that self-reliance is the interesting part. Camshafts replaced by
          pneumatic actuators. A gearbox removed rather than improved. A third damper spanning
          the rear axle so the car can be soft in roll and stiff in heave at the same time.
          Output is counted in dozens of cars a year, which is roughly what it costs to work
          that way.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="story__media reveal" data-reveal-delay="2">
        <Image
          src={storyImg}
          alt="A red Koenigsegg Regera at speed on a coastal road at sunset, waves breaking behind it"
          widths={[560, 900, 1400]}
          sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 45vw"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>The Regera — one fixed ratio, three electric motors, no gearbox.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Principles ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader id="principles-heading" eyebrow="How it works" title="Three habits that explain the cars" class="reveal">
        Not a mission statement — just the three things that keep turning up when you read
        about how a Koenigsegg gets made.
      </SectionHeader>

      <ul class="principles">
        {
          principles.map((p, i) => (
            <li class="principle reveal" data-reveal-delay={i + 1}>
              <p class="principle__n" aria-hidden="true">{p.n}</p>
              <h3>{p.title}</h3>
              <p class="principle__body">{p.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Timeline ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section--deep" aria-labelledby="timeline-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <SectionHeader id="timeline-heading" eyebrow="Milestones" title={`${yearsRunning} years, five moments`} class="reveal" />

      <ol class="timeline">
        {
          milestones.map((m) => (
            <li class="timeline__item reveal">
              {/* The marker is sized by its own content. The old build gave it a
                  fixed 28px circle, which clipped "1994" down to "994". */}
              <div class="timeline__marker">
                <p class="timeline__year">{m.year}</p>
                <span class="timeline__rail" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </div>

              <div class="timeline__card">
                <h3>{m.title}</h3>
                <p>{m.body}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Figures ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section figures" aria-labelledby="figures-heading">
    <div class="container figures__inner">
      <SectionHeader
        id="figures-heading"
        eyebrow="By the numbers"
        title="Three numbers that cover it"
        class="reveal"
      />
      <div class="figures__grid">
        <Counter value={yearsRunning} label={`Years since ${FOUNDED}`} />
        <Counter value={models.length} label="Models in this collection" />
        <Counter
          value={Number(record.value.replace(/,/g, ''))}
          label="Verified two-way record"
          unit={record.unit}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── CTA ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <Cta title="Spotted something wrong?">
    This is an independent tribute build, not a Koenigsegg channel — so corrections,
    questions about how the site was made, and work enquiries all land in the same inbox.
    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <Button href="/contact" variant="primary" icon="arrow-right">Get in touch</Button>
      <Button href="/collection" variant="secondary">Browse the collection</Button>
    </Fragment>
  </Cta>
</Base>

<style>
  /* ---- story ---- */
  .story {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
    /* start, not center — the text column is taller, and centring it left a
       large gap under the photo. */
    align-items: start;
  }

  .story__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .story__text p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    max-width: var(--container-text);
  }

  /* Two classes, so this outranks `.story__text p` on specificity rather
     than relying on source order. */
  .story__text .story__lead {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--gold);
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
  }

  .story__media :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    /* An outline sits outside the box without taking layout space, so the
       old offset "accent frame" cannot push into the copy column. */
    outline: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    outline-offset: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .story__media figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
  }

  /* ---- principles ---- */
  .principles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 280px), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-md);
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .principle {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-neutral);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    transition:
      border-color var(--duration-base) var(--ease-smooth),
      translate var(--duration-base) var(--ease-smooth);
  }

  .principle:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }

  /* Transform-only hover: guard it so the lift does not stick after a tap
     on touch devices. The border-colour feedback above stays unguarded. */
  @media (hover: hover) {
    .principle:hover {
      translate: 0 var(--hover-lift);
    }
  }

  .principle__n {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-2xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .principle h3 {
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
  }

  .principle__body {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
  }

  /* ---- timeline ---- */
  .timeline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .timeline__item {
    display: grid;
    /* `auto` lets the year pill be exactly as wide as its digits. */
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-md);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .timeline__marker {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .timeline__year {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-normal);
    color: var(--gold);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    white-space: nowrap;
    padding: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-xs);
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
  }

  /* The connecting rail is a flex child, not an absolute overlay — it can
     only ever occupy the marker column. */
  .timeline__rail {
    flex: 1;
    width: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgb(var(--gold-rgb) / 0.5), rgb(var(--gold-rgb) / 0.05));
  }

  .timeline__item:last-child .timeline__rail {
    display: none;
  }

  .timeline__card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-neutral);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    transition: border-color var(--duration-base) var(--ease-smooth);
  }

  .timeline__card:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }

  .timeline__card h3 {
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
  }

  .timeline__card p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
  }

  /* ---- figures ---- */
  .figures__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .figures__intro {
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-widest);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .figures__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 200px), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }




  /* ---- responsive ---- */
  /* The three principle cards use auto-fit, which drops to two columns
     around ~970px and orphans the third on its own row. Hold a real
     three-column row past that point... */
  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .principles {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .story {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-xl);
    }
  }

  /* ...then stack to one once three no longer read at width. Placed after
     the three-column rule above so it wins at equal specificity. */
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .principles {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  /* Same three-item orphan for the figure counters (auto-fit collapses to
     two near ~730px) — keep the compact three-across row a while longer. */
  @media (max-width: 740px) {
    .figures__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .timeline__item {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-xs);
    }
    .timeline__marker {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
    }
    .timeline__rail {
      flex: 1;
      width: auto;
      height: 1px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgb(var(--gold-rgb) / 0.5), rgb(var(--gold-rgb) / 0.05));
    }
    .figures__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
